{"title":"2013 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 2c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb3ddf9a5fa2fca5c4787d4f989af0eef1387bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4b41dd37dcc418b2bd81d72c4d763936a2fc76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/0/1d059b0aed5df7e8a36e8400167d9b5c04a80878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />, and the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is 84. Determine the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The perimeter of a shape is the sum of the lengths of its sides, so we want to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> of a triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/819703adff2d81958bedac48a2bf62fa8ee0bb18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times b \\times h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the base of the triangle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the height of the triangle, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c52e8bce7e119c877549c0e5b4ed3f06ca1e73d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times AH \\times BC = A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a712256cd87cb6e1d2c995c7b0c0c8ec2b5ed18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times 8 \\times BC = 84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"140\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/8/b18bf1c2d5427499a871bf92a3ec27f9acd5b00f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4BC = 84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5a55d46401a0a0561817f47a01fb6ea6272b1dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = \\frac{84}{4} = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Next, we can use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">pythagorean theorem</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/d/4ed19718d84ea66bd08cd0ce70a5a9350d58c6c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABH$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> because it is a right triangle.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b763ebdc682d9953975574f61bf6346ce419a3e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH^{2} + AH^{2} = AB^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/b/f6b67d08e28e25b2cab293e2f12e92f7f3758ec4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH^{2} + 8^2 = 10^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/2/8927c1ad51d77db36da2946b469c282d9fea2f57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH^{2} + 64 = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/f/48f1acb8d571338f1a3b61779ed55010b203a52f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH^{2} = 100 - 64 = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/1/df1548afb947d1e8771214960104050048a69c71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH = \\sqrt{36} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Alternatively, we could have realized that the triangle would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the sides of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/d/32d356c0f30284f26673c9d697124e791b058125.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH = 3 \\times 2 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> can be split into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bfc6159e268a0f5d736eca73477c99a13209da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e8e26d580012b86d8fe55e70e5740908c35af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb8f7215f469843833daa5c650268699b3940e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH + CH = BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/646c5f35c47b67920e4effaea72f374449d7831d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH + 6 = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/3/523d709de0630744ef68bc42632a7e72059ae03e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH = 21 - 6 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>We can then use the pythagorean theorem again with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/b/eabc00e3e07090a48a3155e93649e2aee77a368e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACH$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa034532836276d4f053eaaa671527f1d1de7dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH^{2} + CH^{2} = AC^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/4/dd47120ddf655261d1e67a9d7915ef7979e4c29d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8^{2} + 15^{2} = AC^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/0926aedf8118182fbe70db80b3797f3b695e19f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC^{2} = 64 + 225 = 289$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/3/d234c7f73fccd3209d3636a42fd7af0a43d18850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = \\sqrt{289} = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Alternatively, we could have used the fact that the right triangle was a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> triangle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/f/32ff6896ac10b4da9f3df84c2bccc3893cab6f5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/f/32ff6896ac10b4da9f3df84c2bccc3893cab6f5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/3/5f3773a9dd463d432a5db834e0b94030c0f74f29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b5b6b078188523fb69a22aff2fbd2b3df42b14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, so the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/d/63d0838b88fc6a4836d43a329a0182743a90df5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17 + 21 + 10 = 38 + 10 = \\boxed{48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"237\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017232345\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.074 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 187/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1043/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8761/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   18.965      1 -total\n 31.62%    5.997      1 2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2\n 29.39%    5.574      3 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36035:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017232345 and revision id 279707. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}